[%# The discovery ports, beside the streaming port.  DLNA clients find the
    server with SSDP on 1900/udp.  Local Plex servers and clients find each
    other with Plex GDM on 32410, 32412, 32413 and 32414/udp.  32469/udp is the
    DLNA server.  Without these ports, a client that knows the address can
    connect, but nothing on the LAN can find the address.

    These ports are always open, with no flag to close them.  A media server
    that nobody can find is the usual failure.  If somebody does not want GDM
    and DLNA on their LAN, add a flag then. -%]
[plexmediaserver]
title=Plex Media Server
description=Plex personal media streaming server
ports=32400/tcp|1900,32410,32412,32413,32414,32469/udp
